418 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (1.4 Why Biomass Briquetting?  Loose biomass materials \(carbonized or uncarbonized form\)  cannot give a good quality combustion when applied as an  alternative energy source for domestic and industry use. Thus, to  make effective use of biomass materials, briquetting is employed  to improve the handling characteristics of the biomass material,  increase the volumetric value, and make it available for a variety  of applications. In addition, briquettes possess high burning  efficiency due to its low moisture content and high density.  Therefore, they have higher practical thermal value and much  lower ash content though their efficiency depends on the nature of  materials. )
/E (1.4 Why Biomass Briquetting?  Loose biomass materials \(carbonized or uncarbonized form\)  cannot give a good quality combustion when applied as an  alternative energy source for domestic and industry use. Thus, to  make effective use of biomass materials, briquetting is employed  to improve the handling characteristics of the biomass material,  increase the volumetric value, and make it available for a variety  of applications. In addition, briquettes possess high burning  efficiency due to its low moisture content and high density.  Therefore, they have higher practical thermal value and much  lower ash content though their efficiency depends on the nature of  materials. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
