<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Raw materials that contain high levels of moisture should be dried  before pyrolysis or carbonization process. Moisture content of  biomass material should be less than 12%. Drying helps to remove  excess moisture, which can lead to long carbonization time and  reduction of the efficiency of carbonization process. For fecal  sludge, dewatering should be employed to reduce large quantity  of water before drying process. )
/E (Raw materials that contain high levels of moisture should be dried  before pyrolysis or carbonization process. Moisture content of  biomass material should be less than 12%. Drying helps to remove  excess moisture, which can lead to long carbonization time and  reduction of the efficiency of carbonization process. For fecal  sludge, dewatering should be employed to reduce large quantity  of water before drying process. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
