/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (2.5.3 Open Air Drying  This involves leaving the briquettes in a well-ventilated area to dry  naturally \(Figure 2.9\). The briquettes are placed on racks or hung up  in a dry, cool place where air circulates around them. This method  can take several days, depending on the humidity levels and  temperature. )
/E (2.5.3 Open Air Drying  This involves leaving the briquettes in a well-ventilated area to dry  naturally \(Figure 2.9\). The briquettes are placed on racks or hung up  in a dry, cool place where air circulates around them. This method  can take several days, depending on the humidity levels and  temperature. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [5]
