/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (b. Castor: It is a plant that is grown for its oil-rich seeds. The oil can be used as a binder material in biomass briquetting. In addition, the binder material can also be extracted from the seed cake that is left over after the oil has been milled. However, one of the disadvantages of using castor is that the plant is toxic to humans and animals if ingested. This means that care must be taken during the milling process to ensure that the binder material is free from toxic compounds, )
/E (b. Castor: It is a plant that is grown for its oil-rich seeds. The oil can be used as a binder material in biomass briquetting. In addition, the binder material can also be extracted from the seed cake that is left over after the oil has been milled. However, one of the disadvantages of using castor is that the plant is toxic to humans and animals if ingested. This means that care must be taken during the milling process to ensure that the binder material is free from toxic compounds, )
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [2]
>>
